  "question": "Aspirin disables a platelet for its whole life. Platelets live about 10 days, replaced steadily. How many days until half are new?",
  "value": 5,
  "unit": "days",
  "answer": "50 / 10 = 5 days.",
  "move": "Ask whether a drug's effect lives in the blood or in what it touched.",
  "trap": "Answering in hours, since aspirin itself leaves the blood within an hour.",
  "hint": "Platelets have no nucleus, so a blocked one is never repaired; count replacements.",
  "steps": [
    "Platelets live about 10 days, so about 10% are replaced each day, the oldest first.",
    "Half the platelets is 50%.",
    "50 / 10 = 5 days."
